{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/13707-one-off-antagonists-a-brainstorming-thread","id":13707,"title":"One-off antagonists: A Brainstorming thread","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Hunter: The Vigil"],"posts":[{"date":"2013-11-18T17:32:26-08:00","id":13707,"title":"One-off antagonists: A Brainstorming thread","content":"Hi Folks,<br /> <br /> With the talk about &quot;Threats Unknown&quot; on this forum, I was reminded of a thread that was in the old &quot;World of Darkness&quot; forum on the WW site. It was a thread where you just posted weird and slightly creepy locations that you could set scenarios or scenes in; it turned out to be very popular and had over 100 entries before it ran out of steam. By way of example, here's one of them:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <b>Classroom 213: </b>On the edge of town is an old school house. The place is still in use as a public elementary school. If you break in and get to room 213 on the second floor, sit down in the center desk and wait two hours without saying anything. If you do it right, you'll hear invisible nails scratching against the chalkboard of the class room. </div> </div> </div>The thread is here: <a href=\"http://forums.white-wolf.com/default.aspx?g=posts&amp;m=86142\" target=\"_blank\">http://forums.white-wolf.com/default...=posts&amp;m=86142</a><br /> <br /> I thought it would be pretty awesome to come up with a similar thing for Hunter antagonists - just a very short (2-3 sentence) description of a threat, or rumours of a threat, that ST's can take a run with, adding it to their campaign as needed. I'll kick it off:<br /> <br /> <b>The wall</b><br /> Somewhere in the middle of town, in a run down alley, there is a wall with ever-changing grafitti on it. No one knows who does the paintings - there never seem to be any witnesses to the scenes changing. The pictures are sometimes so abstract as to be undecipherable; other times they clearly show a person, or a place. What no one has yet figured out is that the scenes shown on the wall are premonitions - whoever or whatever is shown on the wall disappears within 48 hours. Late at night the drifters and homeless that live in the alleyway hear distant screaming, as if the wall itself is trying to scare them of. Or maybe warn them?<br /> <br /> <i>Possible Explanations</i><ul><li>The wall is sentient, and is displaying these images as a warning to those who can see it</li> <li>There is a madman with an artistic flair in the city, who paints these images as a way of preparing for his next kidnapping/theft</li> <li>The wall is a glitch in the God Machine, and is displaying images from the near future before they are added to the world</li> <li>Something else...</li> </ul>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":568,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/568-viperion","user":"Viperion","date":". 11-18-2013, 08:35 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/568-viperion","name":"Viperion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar568_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"73"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-19T12:45:52-08:00","id":14229,"title":"","content":"<b>Ward 13</b><br /> In the city's central hospital, there's a ward which is rarely spoken of. It's cursed, some say. The mortality rate in Ward 13 is far, far higher than any other although there <span style=\"font-family:arial\">seems to be no pattern to the deaths save one; the most common cause of death is complications from surgery leading to a massive brain h</span><span style=\"color:#252c2f\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">emorrhage and brain death. For obvious reasons this high death rate is kept as low profile as possible, but some doctors are now refusing to operate on patients from Ward 13 for fear of losing their patient.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:arial\"><i>Possible Explanations</i></span></span></span><ul><li><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><span style=\"color:#252c2f\">There is a spirit of knowledge trapped in the ward somehow; it must survive by draining the thoughts and memories of it's victims.</span></span></li> <li><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><span style=\"color:#252c2f\">One of the night staff has gone mad, and is attempting to harvest organs to create a Promethean, or perhaps simply to feast on. They have discovered a near-undetectable drug that creates the hemorrhage but leaves the body's main organs undamaged. (<i>Follow up hook</i>: Who is supplying the drug, and what are <i>they</i> getting out of it?)</span></span></li> <li><span style=\"font-family:arial\">An infestation of Brain Worms* are in the ward, finding recovering surgical patients a ridiculously easy target to feed on. It's only a matter of time before they spread to other areas of the hospital</span></li> </ul><span style=\"font-size:9px\">*No, I have no idea what a Brain Worm is. That's up to the ST <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\"><b>Note: </b>Although both of these so far are locations, it's the &quot;Thing&quot; at/causing the location which is important. Some things will be location based (as these are) others will be more &quot;wandering monster&quot; types.</span></span>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":568,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/568-viperion","user":"Viperion","date":". 11-19-2013, 03:48 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/568-viperion","name":"Viperion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar568_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"73"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-19T17:55:03-08:00","id":14406,"title":"","content":"<b>The Cabin Outside of Town</b><br /> In the forest in past the edge of town, there's a small wood cabin with the door and all the windows boarded up. The forest around the cabin is clearly ill; the trees seem to be dying, the ground is a disgusting mush, and nothing seems to prosper other than an unpleasant fungus. There have been a handful of disappearances in the area over the past few decades, which have given generations of kids fodder for urban legends. The thing is, more people seem to be going missing around the cabin than ever before.<br /> <br /> <i>Possible Explanations:</i><ul><li>A Promethean has stalled in his Pilgrimage, afraid of the outside world. He sealed himself inside the cabin long ago, and rarely ventures out for food. The fungus and disappearances are the result of the Wasteland created by the poor creature.</li> <li>The cabin is a piece of Infrastructure, though its purpose is unknown. The fungus in the nearby forest is harmless, but tainted by the machinations of the God-Machine; when inhaled, the spores create a benign infection that allows the host to perceive the servants and gears of the Machine.</li> <li>There exists a portal into the Hedge within the cabin, constructed and sealed sometime ago by Changelings in order to keep people safe. Their plan was not completely effective, however; the energies of the Hedge bleed through into the nearby fungus, and those who stray too close are snatched by the Fae.</li> </ul>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-20T14:06:24-08:00","id":14872,"title":"","content":"<i>(Note: I realise this one isn't exactly a new concept)</i><br /> <br /> <b>The Cult of Beauty</b><br /> &quot;Take years off your appearance!&quot; the ads say. &quot;Only 4 easy payments of $49.99!&quot;. &quot;Come and see our beauty professionals now!&quot; And it sure seems to work. Those who go really do seem to have less wrinkles, sparkling eyes and teeth, and lustrous, shiny hair. Only there's something funny going on - their skin seems to have this waxy, plastic look, and no one will talk about what the treatment actually entails...<br /> <br /> <i>Possible Explanations: </i><ul><li>It's actually totally legit. The waxy look to the skin is a treatment that must be applied daily, and washes off in a nice hot shower. This is a good one to throw at your players if they're overly suspicious and you want to throw a red herring at them</li> <li>It's an operation being run by priestesses of Hathor/Aphrodite/Venus. Again the treatment is actually legit, but in this case the priestesses (and associated God) are gathering power from the devotions and rituals being unwittingly performed by the customers. What the customers (and most of the priestesses) don't know is that they are trading in years at the end of their life for years now - pretty soon now the older patrons will begin dying of heart attacks and internal organ failure - way too soon for it to be happening, but at least they're leaving a good looking corpse..</li> <li>It really is a cult. The customers come and are hypnotised into a slumber while the creature feeds on them. Once it looked almost human, but now it consists of a mass of fat tissue, decaying flesh and pustules of other bodily tissues and fibres. Each time it feeds, it gets stronger, and soon it will be able to feed directly off humans without any assistance or subterfuge. <b>Fat for the Fat God!</b></li> </ul>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/568-viperion","name":"Viperion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar568_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"73"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-21T17:35:10-08:00","id":15733,"title":"","content":"<b>Shadowkin</b><br /> That feeling you get in a not-quite-dark room, when you swear those shadows, half seen, are moving by themselves. The shiver that runs down your spine for no reason. The unnatural cold you feel whenever you walk past that particular alleway. These can all be signs of the Shadowkin, beings that exist only in two dimensions. While capable of independant movement, they far prefer to hop a ride in someone else's shadow - the only indication that someone is being ridden this way is a distinctive shiver that runs up their spine when their shadow and the Shadowkin merge. Very little is known for sure about these elusive beings, and it has proven impossible to capture one (how do you hold something that has no substance?) Even less is known about their motives, their desires or their reason for existence.<br /> <br /> <i>Possible Powers</i><ul><li>Shadowkin can read the thoughts of any sentient being they are merged with</li> <li>They are able to implant suggestions or compulsions while merged, usually while the host is sleeping</li> <li>They can feed off fear and get stronger when exposed to panic</li> <li>The very strongest of Shadowkin can create shadows of their own, in any shape they desire</li> <li>They can give their hosts nightmares and use that fear to feed off</li> <li>They are immune to virtually all attacks, save extremely bright light</li> </ul>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/568-viperion","name":"Viperion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar568_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"73"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-23T17:08:17-08:00","id":16872,"title":"","content":"<b>Duckless Pond</b><br /> <br /> Hey what is the deal with that pond just outside the park entrance? It used to one of the ten hippest Duck feeding spot for spinsters ages 62-84, but the last month or so there are no ducks anywhere near it! Its like they are boycotting the pond or something! Most folks are pleased with just moving over to the other duck ponds but there seems to be always one or two really ancient biddies still tossing crumbs to the pond, they must just be stubborn. Something else isn't right though, no living thing seems to want go near the pond, not dragonflys or any other pond enjoying critter. The real weird thing is while nothing alive seems to be in the pond anymore well past dusk some people have said they see strange ripples and bubbling coming from the pond, often after one of the sentinel crones has somehow disappeared while the viewer was tying their shoe or texting.<br /> <br /> Possible explainations:<ul><li>Hey its a nice pond to sit at, maybe the Ducks left and these old ladies just want to sit by a damned pond, they don't have to answer to you. And ponds bubble, maybe its a mole drowning or something.</li> <li>The Pond's Hungry! Maybe the old ladies are physical manifestations of the Pond meant to lure in food, its eaten all the ducks and maybe now the old ladies try to toss in unsuspecting park goers?</li> <li>Maybe the pond leads to a Trod in the Hedge and the old women are fetches left by a Keeper with thing for grannies.</li> <li>Maybe the ducks used to guard our world from whatever is on the other side of the Pond. Maybe the Old Woman poisoned the pond to remove the feathery wardens of their murky patron and now they gather at the pond to listen to the whispered promises of what they have to gain by helping what dwells on the other side.</li> <li>The old ladies are ghosts. Someone made a habit of preying on the parks elderly patrons and dumping them into the pond. For some reason the bottom of the pond drags the corpses down and doesn't let them go. Now their ghosts haunt their small wet communal grave creeping out the ducks and hoping someone will take notice and bury them proper.</li> <li>Conversely the old women are a small cabal of abmortals tied to the pond, as long as they keep nothing living from entering the pond they can forestall their own deaths indefinitely. But how long can they keep this up?</li> </ul>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-15T20:13:16-08:00","id":30715,"title":"","content":"<b>Odd Station</b><br /> You're flipping through the radio stations while driving around in a hurry, and you stop at an unfamiliar station. What catches you is a very familiar voice. It couldn't be but you get this feeling like its someone doing an excellent impersonation of you? But wait he outright introduces himself as you! He's requesting his favorite song or giving unusually salacious banter about you're significant other to the annoying Radio Host. What's the deal? He's even responding similar to you but with certain facts just off, such as a new promotion when really you're laid off or talking about a deceased relative as if they were still around. What the hell? What's the number to this station you have to get to the bottom of this.<br /> <br /> Possible explanations:<ul><li>Maybe the person calling in is the real you and you're a Fetch? Sucks to be you I guess.</li> <li>Is a Mage ritualistically stalking you, and engineering this even just to psychologically unravel you?</li> <li>You're Car is haunted, perhaps the ghost wishes to distract you so you get in an accident, or even to instill the right emotions.</li> <li>You have driven to a peculiar spot and intercepted the radio signal from another world that is slightly off this world's history. Maybe it's even the true history and the world you live in is the altered world?</li> </ul>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-22T20:24:22-08:00","id":35332,"title":"","content":"<b>That Dog</b><br /> You thought the dog was something you had left behind, a childhood nightmare from your childhood home. The dog wasn't why you moved away, or at least, it wasn't the <i>only</i> reason. But damn if that dog didn't make it an easy decision. It was some kind of mongrel, maybe part beagle, mostly brown with thin patchy hair and prominent ribs. It never barked or growled or snarled, but you used to catch it looking at you. Just staring. You saw it at school first. At lunch time. Just sitting in the grass outside. It was at home after that. Stood on the opposite sidewalk all day. By sunset it was in your yard. In the early hours of the morning you heard a scratching and a whining. You shivered and stumbled to the window. The dog stared at you with golden eyes like glaring headlights, blinding you. Its jaw opened like a snake and its bloated tongue hung out over his blackened and rotted teeth. You closed the curtains lay awake in bed. You laid awake almost every night after that, just listening to the scratching. When you left, you thought it had stayed behind. You thought it might get to your parents. You felt guilty about that for a while. Until your girlfriend found that stray. You told yourself it was an uncanny resemblance. Put the dog outside and laid down to keep your girlfriend warm. And then the scratching started again.<br /> <br /> <i>Possible Explanations</i><ul><li>That dog has been stalking people since your town was founded. The settlers took their dogs into the woods, and a hound returned without the hunters. It was covered in strange bites and died within the week. They buried it past the treeline. But they had to expand eventually. It's never had to chase anyone this far before, but it's willing.</li> <li>The girlfriend summoned the creature years ago, just to lead you to her. It's here now, purpose fulfilled. Is she a lonely witch? A stupid girl meddling with forces beyond her control? Or something ancient, immortal, and hungry? Even if the girl's ends are benign, the dog may not be dismissed willingly.</li> <li>The dog is infrastructure, a canid angel with fluorescent eyes and a thin coat of false hair, chasing you to your destiny, furthering the will of the machine in the cracks of reality. What will you do when you find out the dog wants you to do something terrible? What will you do when you find out you have no choice?</li> </ul>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1063,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1063-kajedhorrors","user":"kajedhorrors","date":". 12-22-2013, 11:26 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1063-kajedhorrors","name":"kajedhorrors","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"22"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-03T04:15:03-08:00","id":41632,"title":"","content":"<b>The Town Founders</b><br /> Why is it the leading council of the heads of the Town Businesses look just like the black and white photos of the town founders? Are they just the descendants of them as many claim to be? Maybe the town just attracts old style beard enthusiasts? That seems weird because only half them claim to be descendants the others don't have any claims to a legacy whats so ever. While they aren't billionaires, and really I'm not sure any have over a million dollars they seem to hold the towns fate in their collective hands. Its strange most seem to be Bachelors and Widows, and traditionally have been according to the research you have done, so why do they seem to always get replaced with descendants previously unknown by anyone? And they always number in 13, that seems like a rather particular number...<br /> <br /> <i>Possible Explanations</i><ul><li>They are a group of Immortals who have chosen to carve out a tiny kingdom out of this tiny territory. Perhaps they are literally as eternal as the town itself and they cannot leave?</li> <li>Maybe they are a collection of spirits or claimed or even ghost possessed individuals? Perhaps even representing the town and local businesses?</li> <li>Perhaps the council represents a senate of priests with the mayor as the sole priest to the king of some head god of a lost pantheon, reflecting the in the living/material world what is reflected in the other world?</li> <li>Perhaps they are alchemical clones recreated regularly over the years to guide the town to a prophetic future as a utopia or apocalypse?</li> <li>Maybe they are just weird group of rich old white folks that made some strange tradition/secret society to emulate their predecessors for kicks, or just out of some sort of luck/superstition.</li> </ul>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-03T14:32:29-08:00","id":41956,"title":"","content":"<b>Bloody Mess</b><br /> <br /> There's a spot in the park where it looks like everything is covered in blood. Old concrete blocks are covered in streams of rust, red flowers bloom, and a fungus the color of dried blood infests the tress. It's also utterly choked with mosquitoes, people will be practically coated with the little things should they wander through this area. Despite the efforts of park staff (or because of neglect) the affected area is expanding. Worse, several park-goers have come down with a painful, bleeding rash.<br /> <br /> <i>Possible Explanations</i><ul><li>The cause is perfectly mundane - an ordinary fungus is feasting on chemicals illegally dumped here, and ideal conditions exist for mosquitoes to spread a nasty bacteria.</li> <li>A creature was buried here by other hunters, who dumped it without performing the necessary rituals to properly destroy the entity. Too damaged to escape and in too much pain to think clearly, the half-dead creature writhes in it's shallow grave while it's ichor pollutes the area.</li> <li>Someone is cultivating this place to be the site of a future ritual. Everything here has been designed to evoke 'blood' from the flowers, insects, and irritants seeded at bus stops and park benches. At the next lunar eclipse when the moon turns red, the ritual will be performed.</li> <li>An injured vampire sunk into the ground here. Starved and almost comatose, the broken body attracted mosquitoes and became their nest, even as the vampire exerted his will upon them in turn. When the insects feed, a few drops of blood are tithed to their new 'home.' When the vampire finally has enough blood to heal himself, a new and very dangerous form of vampire will begin stalking the city, a living hive full of blood-stealing insects.</li> </ul><br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1457-quanutmshard","name":"Quanutmshard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1457_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"61"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-04T11:16:19-08:00","id":42361,"title":"","content":"<b>The Trucker</b><br /> He's seen most of America, because he always takes the longest routes. He's always on time. He never sleeps.<br /> Well, sometimes he has to, in cheap motels between jobs, when the pills run out. He doesn't like it, though, because his sleep brings bad things with it, and death is the least of them.<br /> <i>Possible explanations:</i><ul><li>The trucker's dreams are the gates of a prison, a black place where wicked things dwell. When he sleeps, the gates are wide open; when he dies, they'll never close again.</li> <li>He should really be sleeping more. As it is, his weary brain has to take other people's sleep, and it's not very delicate about it.</li> <li>The stimulant he takes to stay awake has a side effect: when it runs out, his mind goes elsewhere, leaving his body an empty suit of meat. There are lots of ghosts and demons in the old motels, it seems.</li> </ul><br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/97-the-mg","name":"The MG","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar97_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2460"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-04T14:22:06-08:00","id":42478,"title":"","content":"Whoah I was going to comment on the Bloody Mess one being a great one to use, but Damn The Trucker is real homerun!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-05T13:31:26-08:00","id":43097,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eldagusto</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/13707-one-off-antagonists-a-brainstorming-thread?p=42478#post42478\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Whoah I was going to comment on the Bloody Mess one being a great one to use, but Damn The Trucker is real homerun!</div> </div> </div> </div>Totally agree I'm stealing both of these to use in my game <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> Thanks guys!<br /> <br /> Let's keep 'em coming!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/568-viperion","name":"Viperion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar568_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"73"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-09T19:52:39-08:00","id":46011,"title":"","content":"<b>The Giant of Filth and Refuse.</b><br /> <br /> &quot;<i>It's a bit of a local legend now. I guess I am too.</i>&quot; The man grunts, limping over to the Giant's side. &quot;<i>Tourists love it,</i>&quot; the vagrant sighs wearily.<br /> He reaches a quivering hand towards his creation and brushes his fingers against it. The light rain splatters the man's quivering hand as he runs it down the side of the massive structure. It is a hideous, towering, and vaguely humanoid shape on the side of an old dirt road. It stands a dozen feet tall, made out of pressed mud and a whole lot of garbage. The old man pricks his finger on the jagged edge of a soda can at the giant's hip, but he doesn't seem to notice. He takes a step back, sweeping his sharp but ancient gaze from the sculpture, to you, and then to the large painted sign that identifies the Giant.<br /> &quot;<i>It's not what I would have called it.</i>&quot; The man grumbles. &quot;<i>I might have come up with something more clever, less cumbersome.</i>&quot;<br /> You wonder what that means. You wonder who <i>did</i> name it. You try to ask him. You're not sure you even managed. You stare transfixed at the Giant of Filth and Refuse. At any rate, he doesn't answer. He follows your gaze and stares with you.<br /> &quot;<i>It's almost done</i>.&quot; The man whispers.<br /> Blood drips down his fingers and mingles with the mud at his feet. He reaches down and scoops up a handful of moist earth. He considers it briefly before he presses it gently to the side of the Giant of Filth and Refuse.<br /> <i>&quot;Almost done...&quot;</i><br /> <br /> <i>Possible Explanations</i><ul><li><i>&quot;It was the recruiter, I guess. He told me the army would be good for me. Shipped me across the sea. If it weren't for him I wouldn't be homeless. Wouldn't be mad.&quot; </i>The man was influenced by a supernatural creature a long time ago. It is a patient entity, but it will soon return for its</li> <li><i>&quot;Do you like it? Most people are scared of it. I'm scared of it. Not you though. That's good. It's a gift. It's for you. Yes... I wasn't sure before. But I know it now. It <b>is </b>for you. It's always been for you.&quot; </i>This possibility bothers him almost as much as it bothers you. The sculpture seemed like a waste of life, an endless and pointless endeavor that he couldn't make himself stop. Until you came. It all makes sense now. It is <b>your </b>burden now.</li> <li><i>&quot;Press against the side. Yes, just there. Good... Can you hear it? The pulse. The voice. The life. What's inside? What's inside? Please. Tell me what's inside. Please *Sobs*&quot; </i>The sculpture is the vessel or the body for something ancient and infant. Great and terrible. It will soon shamble forth. The giant will walk.</li> </ul>(Apologies for the bizarre format of this entry, I just felt it would come out best in this kind of second person narrative.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1063-kajedhorrors","name":"kajedhorrors","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"22"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-10T01:18:44-08:00","id":46137,"title":"","content":"<b>The Whispering Blade</b><br /> <br /> The police (or maybe your cell) arrived just in time. His eighth victim is expected to live, albeit with some horrible scarring and the need of a prosthetic or two. The killers swears that the knife he used in the killings is possessed by a demon, and no matter what he did to get rid of it, the knife would always return. After weeks of hearing the maddening whispers, he couldn't resist anymore and gave in to the terrible demands it made of him. Of course, considering that the killer had a history of schizophrenia, no one is buying it.<ul><li>The man is a schizophrenic and was being treated for it, dutifully taking his medication. He also stood to inherit a rather large sum of money after the death of his father. The man's uncle, after being written out of the will after a falling out with his brother, commissioned a dozen identical knives with hollow handles that held a long-lasting battery, a radio receiver, and a tiny speaker, disguised as a bit of filigree.</li> <li>The blade itself isn't special, but there's a powerful spirit of murder-by-knife that's rather fond of it, and has made use of it for years. The spirit is powerful enough to repair the knife after being destroyed, and arrange events that made sure the knife ended up wherever it wanted. Finding the ignorant wolf-blood was a bonus, he had no idea that the voices in his head were quite real.</li> <li>He's not crazy, he's psychic. Never realizing the nature of his psychometric powers, the doctors diagnosed his visions as schizophrenia, and the pills he was prescribed dulled those brain functions that controlled his powers. All was well and good, until he visited an antique store and became fascinated with a beautiful blade for sale. It had more history than anything else he'd ever touched - centuries of bloody, unholy history, and before it was lost, many have fought to possess it for various reasons. Mere days after images of the blade begin to circulate, either released by the police or during the cell's research of it, a great many new people are going to come to town, and they don't plan to leave without it in their possession.</li> </ul><br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1457-quanutmshard","name":"Quanutmshard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1457_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"61"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-11T03:27:10-08:00","id":46821,"title":"","content":"<b>The Line</b><br /> <br /> In the local park, on a hill away from the built-in grills and pavilions, there is a three foot long by one foot wide slab of cement. On that slab is a red Line about 2 feet long and barely an inch thick. It's been there for as long as any one can remember. The kids will dare each other to cross that Line. It's the dare no one will refuse, but very few ever go thru with, because everybody knows that anyone who crosses the Line will disappear the next day. To cross the Line, it has to be voluntary. If someone pushes you over the Line, it doesn't count.<ul><li>The Line is a weak point between the material world and the Shadow Realm. There is a magath that lives there that began as a spirit of bravery, which is why only those who are dared and cross the Line of their own free will are taken. Anyone who crosses it under those conditions is compelled to come back again late that night when the Gauntlet is weak. Once they cross the Line again late at night, they will cross fully into the Shadow Realm and fed upon by the magath.</li> <li>The position of groundskeeper at this park has been handed down from father to son to grandson for over 50 years now, and they all have one thing in common: they are all serial killers. They maintain the Line and the legend to help throw off suspicion when they take another kid as a victim. They watch the Line carefully (grandson has installed cameras so he doesn't miss anyone) and take anyone who crosses it, though grandson's constant watching has noticeably increased the number of victims.</li> <li>It started as an attempt by one of the city workers who maintained the park to keep his kids from running over the hill and out of his sight. The current day maintenance crew will refresh the paint on the Line out of habit because it's always been done. The number of disappearances has been exaggerated and it's just a coincidence that some of the kids who crossed the Line have disappeared. A few have even returned, but that's never remembered as well as the disappearance.</li> <li>The slab of cement is a Pandoran in Dormancy. When moon rises after someone has been dared to cross the Line and then goes over it voluntarily, some bizarre Flux ritual becomes fulfilled and grants the Pandoran just enough Pyros (1 point) to get up that evening and go hunting. The Line itself is where the maw of the creature would be, so whomever has crossed the Line has their scent stuck in the creatures nose when it awakes. It awakes thinking that scent is a Promethean to consume. While it has occasionally failed to grab the child who crossed the Line, it's been successful enough to maintain the stories.</li> </ul><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>- If you must be ridiculous, I must ridicule you.<br /> - Those that can give up essential liberties in exchange for temporary safety deserve neither liberty nor safety. -- Benjamin Franklin</i>","edited":{"userid":375,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/375-papa-bear","user":"Papa Bear","date":". 01-11-2014, 06:30 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/375-papa-bear","name":"Papa Bear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar375_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1920"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-11T23:20:52-08:00","id":47269,"title":"","content":"<b>The Collector</b><br /> <br /> Local hunters tell each other stories of the Collector - a quirky little man that can be seen rooting through trash cans, patiently pacing the tables at the flea-market, appearing at every estate sale and auction, and sometimes approaching people and asking if they would be willing to part with a certain item in their possession. More often than not, the item in question seems to be mundane and of low value. A few times, potent mystical artifacts and ancient relics have been pulled from his pockets and traded away for a pittance and a smile.<ul><li>The Collector is a mostly-mundane human, compulsively collecting 'stuff' that he judges important by some unknown criteria. He has a tiny smidgeon of psychic power that sometimes nudges him towards picking up the strange, but he inevitably loses interest in the items he acquires. He pays in cash, and has a talent for cold-reading, forgery and conning people into buying things for far more then they're really worth, which is how he scrapes by.</li> <li>The Collector is a strange fae creature who delights in causing chaos. He always knows exactly the right place and time to add or remove a specific item that will set off a potentially disastrous chain of events with all the ease of a human tipping over a domino. While the item he offers in trade are usually mundane and only triggers an effect based on it's perceived nature as 'proof of infidelity' or 'something to inspire jealousy' he will sometimes pay with fae-forged items, the mystical equivalent of bad pennies that cause minor misfortunes for those that carry or use them.</li> <li>The Collector is a young mage who once stumbled across an enchanted item gathering dust in a secondhand store, and now spends his free time scouring the city with his magic for any other lost gems. Not wanting to put himself in a hunter's crosshairs, he assumed a distinctive disguise with magic when going out on a jaunt, but as a result, spawned the new urban legend currently being spread. In his guise as the Collector (dun-dun-DUN!) he openly trades with those hunters and other creatures that he feels are safe to approach, offering information, services and the odd 'magical item' which are useless placebos. In such cases, the real power comes from the Collector, who works his subtle spells on hunters while they are busy drinking the kool-aid potions, burning the dollar-store incense, or reading gibberish from the 'ancient book of spells.'</li> </ul><br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1457-quanutmshard","name":"Quanutmshard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1457_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"61"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-12T20:27:27-08:00","id":47843,"title":"","content":"<b>Doomtrain</b><br /> <br /> The hunters must investigate when a commuter train with dozens of passengers doesn't reach it's destination. The trip takes them to a rusting industrial area, left behind by the march of process. There's nothing around them for miles, save for rusting steel, fractured concrete, and the detritus of man's passing. Plenty of room here to hide an entire trains and the bodies of the passengers - the question is, who would want to steal a train?<br /> <br /> [ATTACH=CONFIG]n220[/ATTACH]<br /> <br /> bonus: Play this as background music.<br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"http://www.youtube.com/watch?v=pse4gcBprLk\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/google-material/image_placeholder.svg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://www.youtube.com/watch?v=pse4gcBprLk\" target=\"_blank\"> </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://www.youtube.com/watch?v=pse4gcBprLk\" target=\"_blank\"> http://www.youtube.com/watch?v=pse4gcBprLk </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1457-quanutmshard","name":"Quanutmshard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1457_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"61"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-24T20:42:50-07:00","id":98042,"title":"","content":"This thread is great it needs to keep going!<br /> <br /> <b>The Old Goat Farm</b><br /> <br /> The old farm out by Riverston seems normal. Its been owned by multiple families over the last hundred years but they have all been &quot;town families&quot;. If you talk to the old folks around town you can piece together interesting tidbits.<br /> <br /> -Strangest probably would be the fact that the only animals raised on the farm have been goats, no dogs or even cats only goats.<br /> <br /> -There are also a pattern of only single males working the property. Folks have sworn they remember married couples buying the property but everyone seems to only remember seeing husbands,widowers, or other males working the fields, often in flowing hooded robes even under the summers sun's abominable gaze<br /> <br /> -The fields have always seemed particularly fruitful, even when left fallow, wild strawberries and wheat seem to aggregate in the eerie field.<br /> <br /> <i>Possible Explainations and Secret:</i><ul><li>There actually have been other animals raised on the old farm, the thing is all the females seem to get pregnant and only give birth to baby goats. Doesn't matter if its a Mamma milk cow, sow, or sheep dog. One of the issues is small animals such as cats and smaller dogs don't seem able to survive a kid growing within them, inevitably resulting in the death of both the mother and child as the enlarging goat fetus swells too big for the mother to support till she bursts. Farmers quickly learned to not press their luck and raise only goats, which benefit from the fertility. Avoids questions and earns a steady buck.</li> <li>This may also apply to human females, and the history of the farm is riddled with suicides as simple farm folk psyches seem to shatter like dropped glass at the ordeal of birthing goats.</li> <li>Something with cloven hooves dwells within the farms moss covered well, something with red eyes that stinks of sulfur. This lusty devil may be assaulting all the females of farm.</li> <li>The farm was original owned almost two hundred years ago by a family that immigrated from the Mediterranean. They were worshipers of Pan and they consecrated the grounds as temple of Pan, declaring all females as priestess wives of the Goat God. In exchange a boon of fertility is anchored into the very earth.</li> <li>Perhaps a potent brood of Goat spirits of fecundity claims a locus in the old barn. When a family movies in the head of the family quickly becomes one of the Claimed. They tend to keep their wives chained in the basement producing strong horned sons with bandy cloven feet. They wear the hooded robes to conceal their birthright of horns, hooves and tails. The spirits brutally murder all animals that aren't goats.</li> <li>With the deed to the farm comes a simple instruction manual detailing the rites of spring which culminates in the sacrificing of healthy goats, their blood seeping into the shallow grave of a mother who outlived here children. This rite guarantees fortune for the farm, and an easing of physical maladies and the pains that come from old age.</li> <li>Its just a farm for people that love goats, lots and lots of goats. Perhaps the farmers love goats too much...</li> <li>The goats run the farm. Perhaps a breed of cryptid goats that herd a godmachine cult that tend to simple tunnels and expansive underground wells and cellars. Or maybe the goats are immortals in caprine prisons, they puppeteer humans around them for their amusement eventually transmuting them into produce when board or desiring new slaves.</li> </ul><br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-31T11:41:59-07:00","id":214916,"title":"","content":"Just wondering if there are any other ideas akin to what's in this thread? I find this far more approachable (Yes, I know it's different) and less esoteric than the 1001 Hunter Story Hooks thread.<br /> <br /> I love the ideas here. Great work.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2798-ordo-septenarius","name":"Ordo Septenarius","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"55"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}